><surname>Yu</surname><given-names>TS</given-names></name><name><surname>Wong</surname><given-names>AHS</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Association between daily mortalities from respiratory and cardiovascular diseases and air pollution in Hong Kong, China</article-title><source>Occup Environ Med</source><year>2002</year><volume>59</volume><fpage>30</fpage><lpage>35</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11836466</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1136/oem.59.1.30</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mahaswaran</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Elliott</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Stroke mortality associated with living near main roads in England and Wales: a geographical study</article-title><source>Stroke</source><year>2003</year><volume>34</volume><fpage>2776</fpage><lpage>2780</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14615623</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1161/01.STR.0000101750.77547.11</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kaplan</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Kaplan</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><source>The Experience of Nature: A Psychological Perspective</source><year>1989</year><publisher-name>Cambridge: Cambridge University Press</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kawachi</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Kennedy</surname><given-names>BP</given-names></name><name><surname>Lochner</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Prothrow-Stith</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Social capital, income inequality, and mortality</article-title><source>Am J Public Health</